# The lattice meshes and fields are the POINT of §0 but they are not committable:
# arm C's rung-0.68 lattice STL alone is 755 MB — which is itself the maintainer's
# file-size complaint, and why beam-lattice 3MF is worth its own task. Their SIZES
# and every figure derived from them live in s0_table.txt and in the .report.json
# receipts, which ARE committed. Regenerate with the commands in README.md.
*.stl
*_alpha.f64
*_alpha.meta
design.bin
fields.bin
iterations.csv
# The snapshot binary is 2.7 MB. It is identified by its fingerprint instead —
# `topopt-cli --version` prints it, and README.md records which one produced these
# numbers, so a rebuild can be checked rather than trusted.
topopt-cli.snapshot
